=== Playing the scene loop solo
- #strong[See, Rule, Leads:] come from the generators.
- #strong[Want:] roll it for every person on stage before you decide what your character does.
- #strong[Roll:] name the consequence first, using the failure table above.
- #strong[Enemies in combat:] they follow their motive. Each enemy turn, ask the oracle "Does it press the attack?" (likely when winning, unlikely when hurt). On no, it uses its fight-ending condition: flees, bargains, or grabs what it came for.

== Advancement pacing --- Open
Obstacle points are awarded per the player handbook (minor 1, major 2, critical 3). Not yet decided:

- How many points a typical session should award. A session with one major and two minor obstacles gives 4.
- What Fount scores unlock. 4 and 6 already lower spell costs; ability thresholds wait on playtest data.

== Downtime --- Open
The player handbook says changing practiced spells takes "a few days of downtime." Downtime has no rules yet. Candidates: train (practiced spells), work (earn coin by knack or archetype), craft (spell components, gear), research (one true fact, like I Read About This), and carouse (a contact, a rumor, and a consequence).

== Fount twists for places --- Open
Every location has a primary Fount and, one time in three, a secondary twist. The starting-location generator has prompts and one worked pair (left-footed water: ᛄ~Seron with a ⌘~Veyra twist). Still needed: all 20 ordered pairs and five primary-only effects, each with a trigger, outcome, and exploit.

